From: S4 noise slot (claude/s4-noise)
Subject: provision_range takes the reserved noise management addresses

Not applied on claude/s4-noise: worker/worker/tasks.py belongs to another slot.

The API already reserves each noise agent's management address when it accepts a
provision (app/noise/mgmt.py via range_ops.service.accept) and registers agents at
those addresses on deploy. What is missing is handing them to the worker so that
render.py builds the management NICs (render_topology(..., noise_mgmt=...), already
on the branch, and the vSphere NIC build in provisioners/vsphere_api.py).

The API side needs no change: range_ops.service._task_args sends the addresses as soon
as the provision contract declares `noise_mgmt` (_contract_takes). The contract parity
test (tests/contracts/test_task_contracts.py) makes the contract and this signature
land together.

Apply, then regenerate the copies and run the gate:

    git apply .agent-patches/s4-noise-provision-range-mgmt.patch
    .venv/bin/python scripts/export_task_contracts.py   # API copy + worker-tasks.schema.json
    bash scripts/dod.sh

Tests that then exercise the real contract instead of the fixture:
tests/api/test_noise_reservations.py (worker_takes_addresses becomes a no-op;
test_addresses_are_reserved_but_not_sent_while_the_worker_cannot_take_them must be
deleted, it pins today's gap).

